---
// Each column follows one family dependency path to the shared kernel.
---
<figure class="landing not-content mx-auto my-8 max-w-2xl font-mono text-sm">
  <div class="space-y-2 text-center">
    <div class="rounded-xl border px-4 py-3">
      <strong>causa</strong>
      <div class="opacity-70">kernel always on · other layers selected by features</div>
    </div>
    <div class="opacity-70">depends on the selected layers below</div>
    <div class="grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl border px-4 py-3">
        <strong>provider</strong>
        <div class="opacity-70">reqwest gateways</div>
        <div class="my-2">↓ depends on</div>
        <strong>protocol</strong>
        <div class="opacity-70">pure wire translation</div>
        <div class="my-2">↓ depends on</div>
        <strong>kernel</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border px-4 py-3">
        <strong>runtime</strong>
        <div class="opacity-70">optional components</div>
        <div class="my-2">↓ depends on</div>
        <strong>kernel</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border px-4 py-3">
        <strong>extension</strong>
        <div class="opacity-70">MCP tool sources</div>
        <div class="my-2">↓ depends on</div>
        <strong>kernel</strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-center font-sans text-sm opacity-70">
    All three paths share the same kernel. Arrows show normal family dependencies;
    CI checks their direction. No family crate depends on the facade.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
